\subsection{Cadence and normalized regularization corner}
\label{sec:adaptation-rs-scaling}\label{sec:adaptation-cadence}
Holding $\kappa=\omega_R\tau$ fixed would require
\begin{align}
R_S&=\frac{q_{\mathrm{eff}}\tau^6}{T_S\kappa^6},
\label{eq:adapt-RS-general}\\
r_S&=\frac{\sqrt{q_{\mathrm{eff}}}}{\sqrt{c_T}\kappa^3}\tau^{5/2}
\quad(T_S=c_T\tau).
\label{eq:adapt-rs-strong-law}
\end{align}
This preserves a normalized corner but does not minimize physical displacement
error. That optimum must also account for distortion of the desired wave
spectrum, as follows.
